course: dictionary
lesson: 15329
title: Snob: looking down on others
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A snob is a person who thinks they are better than other people and looks down on them. Snobs may judge others by how much money they have, which family they come from, which school they went to, or what class they belong to. The clue is in the looking down: a snob is proud and unkind about it.
explain: «Lily would not play with Sam because his family did not have a big house.» Lily is being a snob. She judges Sam by his house, not by what kind of friend he is. The sentence tells you she is proud and unkind, so the word snob fits her.
explain: The word can also be about taste. «Dad is a coffee snob; he will only drink beans from one shop.» A coffee snob thinks their own choice is best and looks down on other people's choices. Ask yourself: is this person proud and looking down on someone? If yes, snob probably fits.
fact: A snob thinks they are better than others and looks down on them.
fact: Snobs may judge people by money, family, school or class.
fact: «Food snob», «coffee snob» and «book snob» mean someone who thinks their own taste is the best.
fact: «Snob value» means something seems better just because it is expensive or hard to get.
fact: An «inverted snob» looks down on rich or posh things and thinks that makes them better.
exercise: Which word means a person who looks down on others because of money or class? | *Snob | Friend | Helper | Traveller
exercise: «Nina says her cheese is far better than yours and will not even taste yours.» What kind of snob is Nina? | Snob value | Book snob | Sports fan | *Food snob
exercise: Which phrase means someone who looks down on rich or posh things? | Food snob | Coffee snob | Snob value | *Inverted snob
test: «Harry thinks only people from his street are worth talking to.» What does this show about Harry? | Harry is very tired | Harry is kind and generous | *Harry is acting like a snob | Harry is lost
test: A coffee snob thinks their coffee is | Average | *Better than other people's | Cheap and boring | Hard to find in shops
exam: Which sentence best shows a snob? | «The children cheered for their team.» | «Sam shared his crisps with everyone in the class.» | *«Priya would not play with Tom because his family has less money.» | «Lee helped the new girl find her classroom.»
